<Project>
  <!-- A shield, not a configuration.

       Everything under reference/ is a read-only upstream checkout fetched by
       scripts/fetch-reference.cs. Those projects are built with THEIR versioning rules, not this
       repository's, and MSBuild does not know that: Directory.Packages.props discovery walks up
       from each project until it finds one, so a checkout that ships none of its own would find
       the repository root's and inherit central package management from it. Every PackageReference
       with a Version attribute then becomes NU1008.

       That is not hypothetical. ClaudeForge ships a Directory.Build.props and no
       Directory.Packages.props, so scripts/pack-diagnostics.cs failed on every CI job the first
       time this repository had a remote — and only there. On a machine where reference/sources.json
       resolves ClaudeForge to a sibling checkout OUTSIDE this tree, the walk-up never reaches here
       and the pack succeeds, which is why it went unseen through twenty-three plans. Avalonia,
       AvaloniaEdit, DiffPlex and Semi.Avalonia were immune only because each ships its own.

       Setting the flag false stops the search here and hands each checkout back to its own rules.
       This file deliberately declares no PackageVersion items: it is not a place to pin anything. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>false</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
